    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d225-a10">

                <pb facs="0288" n="228" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg228"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 9.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Certificate of Dr. Athey.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Office of Medical Officer in Command</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Marine-Hospital Service</hi></placeName>[, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1894-04-03T23:59:59-05:00"
                            notBefore="1894-03-03T00:00:00-05:00"
                    >undated</date>].</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">To whom it may concern:</p>
                <p>Charles Smith (aged 22 years, born in Sweden, seaman for past three years in
                    United States merchant-marine service on board schooner <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Henry Crosby</hi>) has been for <pb facs="0289" n="229" xml:id="pg229"/>
                    four times and is at present being treated at this office for a wound on hip,
                    which wound, he states, was made by a rifle shot (or ball).</p>
                <p>Treatment began the 3d day of March, 1894. Present condition does not warrant
                    work, and it is impossible to state how long before recovery.</p>
                <closer>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">seal.</hi>] <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >W. L. Athey, M. D.</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">A. A. Surgeon,
                            Marine-Hospital Service</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
